        <h1 class="post-detail__title">Community Foundation's Executive Director</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/49251.webp" alt="Community Foundation's Executive Director" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <h4>CARRIE MOWREY</h4>
<p><span>Executive Director<br />
</span></p>
<p>Carrie Mowrey serves the Community Foundation of Teton Valley as the Executive Director, putting her knowledge of both Teton Valley and the Community Foundation to good use.  Carrie is responsible for the oversight of the annual Tin Cup Challenge, programmatic initiatives, implementation of strategic plans set by the Foundation’s Board of Directors, and executing effective fundraising, marketing and communication plans.</p>
<p>Carrie has been involved with the Community Foundation since 2012, assisting with administration, programs and event coordination. During that time she has played a key role in developing the online Teton Valley Resource Directory, which lists the health and human services available in and around Teton Valley.  She has also organized the Filling the Gaps in Teton Valley Meetings, bringing together the health and human service providers in the region to improve the availability and access to services for local residents.</p>
<p>Originally from Ogden, UT, Carrie earned her bachelor’s degree in Sociology and Women’s Studies from Weber State University. A mother of three young boys, Carrie and her husband, Tim, can be found enjoying many of the local pursuits and activities with their enthusiastic young brood. Carrie is an avid reader of non-fiction, loves the outdoors and thoroughly enjoys the company of the many amazing and talented people she’s met since first moving to the area in 2002.</p>
<p>Please feel free to contact Carrie via telephone at (208) 354-0230 or email at <a title="cmowrey@cftetonvalley.org" href="cmowrey@cftetonvalley.org">cmowrey@cftetonvalley.org</a>.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
